    {
      "description": "flake.lock has five inputs: nixpkgs (nixos-unstable) feeds the dev shell, nixpkgs-images (nixos-26.05) feeds the Nix-built container images, and pyproject-nix, uv2nix and pyproject-build-systems build the Python environments of those images from nix/locks/. All five are re-locked on the Monday schedule of the uv bump, grouped in one pull request and never automerged: the two nixpkgs inputs are rolling channel branches and the other three follow their default branches, so minimumReleaseAge cannot gate the re-lock and a reviewer confirms it",
      "matchManagers": ["nix"],
      "groupName": "nix flake inputs",
      "automerge": false,
      "minimumReleaseAge": "3 days",
      "schedule": ["before 6am on monday"]
    },
    {
      "description": "The Nix spike under nix/spike/ is pinned by hand (nix/spike/README.md): no manager re-locks its flake.lock or edits the generated pyproject.toml and uv.lock files under nix/spike/locks/",
      "matchFileNames": ["nix/spike/**"],
      "enabled": false
    },
    {
      "description": "The locks under nix/locks/ are derived from the release pins by hack/nix-lock.sh (make nix-lock), and the nix-lock-check job fails when they drift: no manager edits the generated pyproject.toml and uv.lock files, which would bypass the generator. ignorePaths keeps the files out of extraction too, so they list no dependency; it repeats the paths of config:recommended's :ignoreModulesAndTests, which a repository value replaces",
      "matchFileNames": ["nix/locks/**"],
      "enabled": false
    },
